# KOVA — New Features, Routes & Components

## Project Structure

```
packages/
  core/           @open-pencil/core — READ ONLY (engine, tools, renderer)
  cli/            headless CLI (ignore)
  mcp/            MCP server (not used by Kova users)
src/
  ai/             AI tool wiring (valibot, not Zod)
  components/
    chat/         AI chat UI
    canvas/       Canvas components
    panels/       Layers + properties panels
  composables/    use-chat.ts and other composables
  views/          Route views
  stores/         Pinia stores
  data/
    campaigns/    Campaign guide .md files (5 types)
desktop/          Tauri v2 — IGNORE entirely
tests/            Playwright E2E + bun:test unit
```

## What Kova Adds

New pages/views:
- /login, /signup — Supabase auth
- /dashboard — client list with email thumbnails
- /clients/:id — brand profile form + email list
- /templates — template browser, filterable by campaign type

New UI enhancements (additive, not replacement):
- Campaign type selector in AI chat panel (dropdown or chips)
- Export panel: section slice lines + per-section PNG/JPEG + ZIP download
- Brand profile form (colors, fonts, logo upload)

New composables:
- useBrandKit(clientId) — loads brand profile, returns formatted prompt string
- useCampaignGuide(type) — loads campaign guide markdown
- useEmailAutoSave(emailId) — debounced Supabase writes with conflict handling
- useGenerationLimit() — checks plan limits before generation

## Routing (Vue Router)

- New routes in src/views/, registered in the router.
- Route protection: unauthenticated -> redirect to /login.
- defineAsyncComponent + <Suspense> for lazy-loaded views.
- Route naming: kebab-case (client-detail, email-editor, template-browser).
- Keep the editor route exactly as OpenPencil defines it.

## VueUse

Already a dependency. Use before writing your own:
useDebounceFn (auto-save), useLocalStorage (UI prefs),
useResizeObserver (canvas panel), useEventListener.

## File Organisation

Each file in order: exported component/composable, subcomponents,
helpers, constants, types/interfaces.
No barrel index.ts unless 3+ exports genuinely always imported together.

## Files You'll Touch Most

src/composables/use-chat.ts    — AI core (see AI Pipeline rule)
src/components/chat/           — Minor: hide provider key, add campaign selector
src/components/                — Add dashboard, brand, template, export components
src/stores/                    — Add user/client/email/brand Pinia stores
src/views/                     — Add dashboard, login, client, template views
src/data/campaigns/            — Write 5 campaign guides (see Campaign rule)

## Deployment

Vite SPA -> Vercel (or Cloudflare Pages).
API routes -> Vercel serverless functions.
Code splitting: defineAsyncComponent for dashboard views to keep editor bundle lean.
No Tauri-specific config, plugins, or imports.

## Testing

Unit: bun:test. Cover composables, utils, buildSystemPrompt(), brand kit formatting.
E2E: Playwright. Cover auth flow, dashboard CRUD, editor route loads.
Run before commits: bun run test:unit && bun run check
